{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop","id":1372903,"title":"Artifact Workshop","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-04T22:37:43-08:00","id":1372903,"title":"Artifact Workshop","content":"I saw a few artifact threads and thought we might want a generalized thread for artifact discussion and workshopping. So, bring us your broken artifacts and vague ideas and let us help you set them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T22:45:36-08:00","id":1372904,"title":"","content":"For the first item, I had an idea earlier for a Green Jade Grimcleaver with evocations that revolve around Introducing Facts and similar things. Attunement bonus would be you get the first evocation \u201cSpeaks for the Trees\u201d free, which would grant a free Lore specialty in Nature or Plants or something. Possibly it could connect with Sorcery via the Root Lore initiation as well.<br /> <br /> ....Unfortunately that\u2019s pretty much all I have for that one. Aside from the pun that got me thinking about it in the first place.<br /> <br /> I mean, I suppose it could let you do something similar to the Lunar medicine charms, where you declare that there are useful medical plants in the area or something or let you animate the trees, but nothing else has quite grabbed me as a good expansion of the central gimmick of Introducing Facts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T00:29:28-08:00","id":1372918,"title":"","content":"Just grilled this up. I'm not especially sure about the mechanics given that I made it in about 5 minutes, but I think the overall idea is okay. Maybe another evocation could be branched off of this to force a target to attempt to challenge a fact somehow? I'm not quite sure how it would work. I could also imagine a higher-level sort of evocation where the wielder plants the grimcleaver into the ground and watches the weapon transform into a tree, the leaves of which can be read to give some sort of Introduce Fact bonus. <br /> <br /> Leaves Know Liars Strike<br /> Cost: 4m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: ???<br /> <br /> Speaks for the Trees has roots that grow deep enough to touch the secret heart of Creation itself, and it hates when humans speak false. With a single strike, it can cleave the body of a liar as easily as shaving a branch from a green sapling.<br /> <br /> This evocation can target only those against whom the bearer has successfully challenged a fact within the last day, or those who attempted to challenge a fact against the bearer and failed. Reroll a number of 6's on Decisive damage rolls equal to the number of successes by which the bearer won the Challenge Fact or Introduce Fact roll against the target until 6's fail to appear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11685-sundance","name":"Sundance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T12:20:56-07:00","id":1374607,"title":"","content":"I've been working on an artifact 3~4 scarf for my sorcerer-priest, but I've been fairly unsure about the fine details, like what it actually <i>does</i>.<br /> <br /> Short version; it's made from the hide of something his past incarnation hunted, stitched with elaborate patterns of Moonsilver threads, and has a prayer written on one side in Starmetal-based ink.<br /> <br /> Long version; &quot;Once, there was a monster. <b>Kalki, the Wave-Trampling Wheel</b> roamed the west, a massive beast that could walk on water, and swim through stone, and in their wake, the Raksha came, dissolving what remained of the islands it ravaged into the stuff of the Wyld. Many inhabited islands were lost to their depredations.<br /> <br /> The Realm drove Kalki back whenever it grew too close to their own holdings. But they would never do more than send it galloping on the underside of the waves, fleeing towards the edges of creation once more. Thus was the eternal dance of dragon and behemoth.<br /> <br /> Until the later days of the Salt Star Rebellion, when Wisteria Voice...&quot;<br /> <br /> (More to be edited in later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 03-25-2020, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T05:22:55-07:00","id":1374743,"title":"","content":"<br /> I think that a link to the previous artifact workshop would be good so here it is: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ation-workshop</a><br /> <br /> For the grimcleaver, I can imagine leaning into the pun even more and giving bonuses to instill and persuade actions dealing with the environment (such as bonuses to flurry with an attack), and an evocation to lift oneself up by the seat f their pants but it does then become a very silly item.<br /> <br /> For the scarf I'd build off the combination of starmetal and the hunt that took place. Evocations would provide help with predicting the behavior of a target that the wielder hunts. Tricks for tracking , sensing motive, and anticipating attacks. <br /> <br /> Edit except you said <u>moonsilver</u> thread and starmetal <u>ink</u> I should learn to read things properly the first time. You could develop evocations, if the wielder isn't a lunar, to emulate traits of the original beast. If the Wielder is a lunar they could devlop evocations that come in useful for getting and utilizing heart's blood shapes - like an evocation that is a new sacred hunt or that gives access to a shape's ability that he or she has not yet purchased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 03-14-2020, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T17:12:51-07:00","id":1375176,"title":"","content":"I had an idea that I didn't know how to balance: An artifact workshop ( :P )<br /> <br /> Something like adding qualities to things created in it or providing assistants. But most of what I was thinking of seemed like it would be better contained in Craft charms, and non-combat artifacts generally don't get much in the way of Evocations anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T03:45:13-07:00","id":1382706,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking mask artifact. Details are still in planning stage and I'm not sure how to balance it reasonable because it's main purpose can be bit niche. It would have two methods of use:<br /> 1. When just carried on person, for example from hanging on belt, it would protect/camouflage from precognition/fate reading and manipulation like effects.<br /> 2. When worn on face, it would help on stealth in sneaking and in resolve and guile what with covering ones face.<br /> <br /> Especially good name ideas are wanted...<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">White Mask</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5-dot artifact, attunement 3</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When worn on face: resolve +1 and guile +2, +2 dice to stealth vs senses beyond human main 5 and to conceal one's identity. Also effect on all social interactions up to storyteller, for example in some situations mask might be inappropriate</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When on person: camouflage ones presence vs all kind of precognition, fate thread readings and such as common normal mortal human. Outside sources trying to affect one's fate is opposite wits+integrity+essence vs manipulating persons manipulation+occult. On successfully resisting, it appears to target as if they successfully affected the mortal camouflage decoy</span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25965-tonkku","name":"Tonkku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:06:47-07:00","id":1383199,"title":"","content":"Some Artifacts I've been considering working on. Need some inspiration for some more evocations and names:<br /> <br /> -A Sling of Distant Surprise, who's form is a sling with a pouch with 5 shards of Jade, one of each color, worked into it (a pattern on the outside). I'm figuring its evocations would give elemental effects to the bullets when thrown. Also working with the idea one starting evocation would make it retain the bullet in the pouch, effectivly turning it into a light meteor hammer melee weapon.<br /> <br /> Oh, and while this has nothing to do with it's powers, I do have the idea that the Dragon Blood who weilds this carries it, when not in use, by tying it around her head and wearing it like a Naruto-style headband (why the jade shards are in a pattern on the outside to make an emblem on her forehead)<br /> <br /> -A combo Artifact, it's a Grand Skycutter that can also be ridden as a Wingboard. Or a Wingboard that can be thrown as a Grand Skycutter. Whichever.<br /> <br /> -An Artifact 5 suit of Armor. Made by or for a First Age Solar who was jealous of the Lunars' being able to transform into a Warform. So, since he can't transform himself his armor transforms around him to create the same effect. Basically, the evocations would be based on transformations to give him enhanced attributes, abilities, &quot;natural&quot; weapons, and so forth.<br /> <br /> And why is it Artifact 5? Because I do have one evocation in mind, it's a high level one and quite a doozy. And I may be thinking to much like a Solar wanting to add it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T23:57:19-07:00","id":1383301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1374607#post1374607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been working on an artifact 3~4 scarf for my sorcerer-priest, but I've been fairly unsure about the fine details, like what it actually <i>does</i>.<br /> <br /> Short version; it's made from the hide of something his past incarnation hunted, stitched with elaborate patterns of Moonsilver threads, and has a prayer written on one side in Starmetal-based ink.<br /> <br /> Long version; &quot;Once, there was a monster. <b>Kalki, the Wave-Trampling Wheel</b> roamed the west, a massive beast that could walk on water, and swim through stone, and in their wake, the Raksha came, dissolving what remained of the islands it ravaged into the stuff of the Wyld. Many inhabited islands were lost to their depredations.<br /> <br /> The Realm drove Kalki back whenever it grew too close to their own holdings. But they would never do more than send it galloping on the underside of the waves, fleeing towards the edges of creation once more. Thus was the eternal dance of dragon and behemoth.<br /> <br /> Until the later days of the Salt Star Rebellion, when Wisteria Voice...&quot;<br /> <br /> (More to be edited in later.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the first question is, is this going to be a Sorcerous Enhancement artifact, a weapon, armor, or something else?<br /> <br /> I like the idea and the backstory. <br /> <br /> I could see it being about a defense from the Wyld or making water and stone take on each other\u2019s properties in some way? Maybe some kind of mobility enhancement? Maybe you can draw motes from water or stone or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T00:23:07-07:00","id":1383302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1383199#post1383199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-A combo Artifact, it's a Grand Skycutter that can also be ridden as a Wingboard. Or a Wingboard that can be thrown as a Grand Skycutter. Whichever.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, just a Windblade from Heirs of the Shogunate, with Blazerider's first custom evocation. Or does the &quot;Grand&quot; refer to making this an oversized version?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1383199#post1383199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-An Artifact 5 suit of Armor. Made by or for a First Age Solar who was jealous of the Lunars' being able to transform into a Warform. So, since he can't transform himself his armor transforms around him to create the same effect. Basically, the evocations would be based on transformations to give him enhanced attributes, abilities, &quot;natural&quot; weapons, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, an update to <b>Deadly Transformation Armor</b>, from BoSVI: Wonders of the Lost Age, in the Power Armor section. Start with Heir's <b>Gunzosha armor</b>, adding Retractable Beast Claws as a custom evocation. Also look to <b>Unison</b> from Arms of the Chosen for its transformation mechanics, and many of its other evocations are appropriate to the theme too. Some filing off of serial numbers may be needed.<br /> <br /> ...Well, that's assuming access to the previews, of course, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-23-2020, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T01:58:00-07:00","id":1383310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1383302#post1383302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just a Windblade from Heirs of the Shogunate, with Blazerider's first custom evocation. Or does the &quot;Grand&quot; refer to making this an oversized version?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Windblade IS a Grand Skycutter. It's an oversized, Heavy weapon, like a Grand Daiklave. Skycutters (and daiklaves) are Medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-23-2020, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T02:13:55-07:00","id":1383314,"title":"","content":"I dont have Heirs to the Shogunate. I missed out on the Kickstarter. So if I'm repeating something that already exists, again, sorry. Nevermind.<br /> <br /> And was there a BoS VI? I assume you mean Books of Sorcery from 2E. Or do you mean BoS I? That is one place I was going to look for lower tier evocations. Though, other stuff to add before the high tier stuff would be fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 04-23-2020, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T06:03:13-07:00","id":1383349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1383314#post1383314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont have Heirs to the Shogunate. I missed out on the Kickstarter. So if I'm repeating something that already exists, again, sorry. Nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is okay. It was a cool idea. So, yeah, <b>Flying Dragon Fang</b> allows Blazerider to be used as a heavy throw weapon --including when being ridden (the rider falls one range band before it returns to catch them)--so it oozes potential as stunt fodder. I can see it basically becoming the default evocation for any windblade.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And was there a BoS VI? I assume you mean Books of Sorcery from 2E. Or do you mean BoS I? </div> </div> </div>Sorry. BoS Vol I.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T18:26:25-07:00","id":1383489,"title":"","content":"Trying to tie off some of my old homebrew shit during the Time of Weirdness. Not sure if this is thread is appropriate to post things that are mostly done but don't warrant their own thread (the old workshop thread seemed to have a mix of both types?), but I threw together a piece <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/ae:final-stroke-longfang\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Final Stroke (Moonsilver Longfang, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> It was in the waning centuries before the Usurpation that the admiral Winter Thorn forged a spear for her reincarnated Solar mate, Aphelion Yestris. Since Yestris was renowned as a wise ruler in her distant Northern domain, Winter Thorn made for her an arbiter's weapon: she offered assembled legal and religious texts from the five directions to the Unconquered Sun in a grand pyre, then blended the ashes with moonsilver to make the shaft, while the head was alloyed with orichalcum from a seal of the Solar Deliberative. In Yestris' hands, the weapon was gentle but firm; but when she was slain by her Dragon-Blooded officers, Winter Thorn fled with the spear to the rim of Creation, and for six centuries it changed hands throughout the Silver Pact, becoming as hard and fierce as their rule. At length it fell to Tepet Arano during a Wyld Hunt along the Black Shale Road, and like Arano himself, it has not been seen since the Tepet's northern legions were routed.<br /> <br /> Final Stroke stands six feet tall, with a smooth silvery surface that widens near the head. Orichalcum filigree spirals from its base to the golden spearhead. Its tip contains a hollowed channel for ink, because the spear is not merely a weapon: it is also a tool for writing.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b> 5m (spear) or 2m (pen)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Medium (+3 ACC, +12 DMG, +1 DEF, OVW 4)<br /> <b>Tags:</b> Lethal, Melee, Thrown (Short), Piercing<br /> <b>Hearthstone slot(s):</b> 1<br /> <b>Era:</b> Thirty Years' Silence <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Evocations of Final Stroke</span></b><br /> <br /> Final Stroke is both a weapon and a tool, and can change in size from a six-foot-long spear to a writing instrument easily held in one hand. Used for writing, its tip can become as supple or rigid as style demands, allowing it to function as either a quill or brush, and it can not only write on any surface in any color of ink but can also write in air with smoke or heatless blue flame that lingers for half an hour. It counts as exceptional equipment for Linguistics, and for Crafts that require a pen or brush, and it retains all these capabilities as a spear.<br /> <br /> A wielder who is skilled with both the spear and pen (having Linguistics \u2022\u2022 and either Melee or Thrown \u2022\u2022) can shift Final Stroke between its two forms as a reflexive action, so long as it is attuned and in hand. It costs two motes to attune as a pen and five as a spear, so when transforming it into a weapon she must make up the difference. As a spear, Final Stroke has a single hearthstone slot beneath its head. The hearthstone remains active while the weapon is changed into a pen, but can only be retrieved by changing it back.<br /> <br /> Some Evocations of Final Stroke can only be used in one of its two forms, and bear an appropriate keyword, <i>Spear-only</i> or <i>Pen-only</i>. Some attacks can be performed with the pen shape. For this purpose, treat that form as an improvised light weapon that may be wielded with Brawl, Melee, Thrown, or Linguistics.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Mark of Reproach</span></span><br /> Cost:</b> \u2014 (2m); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Dissonant<br /> <b>Duration:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> Final Stroke inks a burning brand on an opponent, marking him for death. The Exalt may pay two motes to tag a character with a stroke as a difficulty 2 gambit, or with a character or word at difficulty 3. Re-marking a marked target overwrites the old copy. Against a crashed enemy, a successful gambit costs no Initiative.<br /> <br /> The mark glows when its bearer comes within long range of Final Stroke, imposing a -2 penalty to stealth and disguise. This gambit may even strike dematerialized spirits, rendering them indirectly visible through the mark. Moreover, the Exalt adds one automatic success to rush the marked character or contest his disengage attempts, and when she attacks him with Final Stroke, she may expend the brand in a burning flash, after she hits but before rolling damage, to ignore his Hardness or his soak from armor.<br /> <br /> Unless spent to enhance an attack, the Mark of Reproach cannot be expunged for at least six hours, after which it still requires significant effort to remove.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant:</b> The two-mote cost must be committed to sustain the mark.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Cutting Invective Assault</span></span><br /> Cost:</b> \u2014 (1m per die); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Spear-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mark of Reproach<br /> <br /> The burning of the Mark of Reproach punctuates the end of the culprit's sentence. When she sacrifices the brand to enhance an attack, the Exalt may pay up to (lower of Essence or 3) motes to reroll that many failed damage damage dice. She must pay before the damage is rolled.<br /> <br /> This Charm also allows the wielder to make a Thrown-based <b>decisive</b> attack against a marked target by hurling Final Stroke from up to long range, without needing to aim. If it hits, she <i>must</i> expend the brand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Fierce Heart Mandate</span><br /> Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Beast-King Dictates<br /> <br /> The wielder of Final Stroke needs no other badge of office: her words are law. When she uses Beast-King Dictates (<b>Lunars</b>, p.XX) to enhance written influence penned with the weapon, its cost falls to 3m, and its Protean condition always applies so long as she writes <i>as though</i> she held authority, and believes she has moral or legal grounds to do so.<br /> <br /> These benefits also apply to spoken influence, but only when the Lunar brandishes Final Stroke in its spear form in the thick of combat or some other chaotic scenario.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when the wielder achieves a significant story goal by using Final Stroke.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Racing Hand Poise</span><br /> Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Whirling Brush Method<br /> <br /> A Lawgiver who has mastered the Whirling Brush Method (<b>Exalted</b>, p.322) may apply that uncanny speed and grace to any activity, whether scribing a message or fighting an army. This Charm supplements an action taken with Final Stroke. It removes the Defense penalty for a miscellaneous action or a draw/ready weapon action, and reduces the flurry penalty (for that action only) to -1. If the action also benefits from Whirling Brush Method \u2014 for instance, because the Solar is hurriedly scribing dictation in the midst of a battle \u2014 this Charm is free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Stinging Admonition</span><br /> Cost:</b> 6m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dissonant, Pen-only, Written-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Cutting Invective Assault<br /> <br /> Using Final Stroke, the Exalt pens a short missive designed to unwind the magic of the Mark of Reproach. She must direct it toward either a specific recipient, to anyone bearing a mark, or to anyone with a mark of a specific color. The message may include conventional social influence, but it must have the same targets as the magic.<br /> <br /> When an intended recipient reads the message while bearing a Mark of Reproach, his comprehension catalyzes the mark, blasting it away and inflicting three dice of lethal damage that ignore Hardness. If the message also contained social influence, apply the damage first: any wound penalties it inflicts modify the target's Resolve against the influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> As long as the wielder isn't dissonant with moonsilver, this Evocation awakens at no cost when an enemy escapes bearing the Mark of Reproach despite the wielder's efforts, or when she permits him to escape to focus on more pressing matters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Border-Marking Stroke</span><br /> Cost:</b> 6m, 2i; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Resonant, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until sunrise or sunset<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The wielder traces a long arc along the ground or through the air, marking a boundary with the force of law. She must draw in a continuous motion; if she aims to cover more space than she can cross in a turn, the line ends where she next takes a non-movement action or applies her Defense. One action is enough to fully encircle herself out to the limit of close range, provided there's nothing in her way.<br /> <br /> A curtain of embers rises from the line, extending two range bands vertically. Attacks that cross this curtain in either direction suffer a two-die environmental penalty, and characters (including dematerialized spirits) treat it as difficult terrain. The barrier arcs and crackles when something pushes through it, alerting others to the intrusion. Dematerialized spirits who attempt to cross are rendered visible (though not tangible) until the end of the round where they finish.<br /> <br /> It's also possible to draw a boundary that bars only demons, the undead, and similar creatures of darkness. In this case ranged attacks are not penalized unless the projectile itself is composed of dark energies, like a bolt of necrotic Essence hurled by an Abyssal Exalt.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant:</b> The Charm may be used reflexively after disengaging.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Scorned God Retribution</span><br /> Cost:</b> 1m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Clash, Decisive-only, Perilous, Resonant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mark of Reproach, Border-Marking Stroke<br /> <br /> A law means nothing unless it is enforced. When someone attempts to move or strike through a boundary created with Border-Marking Stroke, the Exalt may detonate that line in a geyser of light and ink, sacrificing it to punish the offender. This is a (Charisma or Intelligence + Linguistics) gambit to add a Mark of Reproach. The Initiative roll succeeds automatically and its cost is waived, although a miss still costs Initiative. If the subject already has a Mark, the attack adds two non-Charm successes.<br /> <br /> If the interloper is trying to cross the line, his movement is cancelled and the gambit functions as an unblockable strike against his Defense. If he is attacking through the boundary, it clashes his attack, regardless of its target or range. Unlike a normal clash, if the enemy wins he must then compare his threshold successes to his target's Defense (though if he attacked the wielder, she suffers the -2 Defense penalty for losing a clash).<br /> <br /> Since this attack originates from the boundary, the wielder's position isn't important, but she must be aware of the intrusion and holding Final Stroke.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant:</b> Every extra success on the attack roll, to a maximum of six, refunds one point of Border-Marking Stroke's cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Draw the Line</span><br /> Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Pen-only, Written-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Any other Evocation of Final Stroke<br /> <br /> Final Stroke binds with chains of ink. The wielder uses it to write a message enjoining its target (whether one person or many) from a specific course of action, as a persuade, bargain, or threaten action. If a target reads the message and it overcomes his Resolve \u2014 even if he resists, and even if it's unacceptable influence \u2014 the weapon plants a thorn of guilt in his heart. If he is caught knowingly violating the ban, Final Stroke is empowered against him, doubling 10s on <b>decisive</b> damage rolls and waiving the Defense penalty for piercing attacks. After the Exalt catches the culprit in the act, this effect fades within a day; otherwise, it lasts indefinitely.<br /> <br /> Only commands <i>not</i> to do something can be enhanced by this Charm. The injunction cannot be overbroad, and it must be less than a Life-Changing Task (<b>Exalted</b>, p.216). &quot;Never go out after dark&quot; or &quot;don't follow me&quot; or are usually acceptable, but &quot;never leave your room&quot; or &quot;don't avoid my attacks&quot; are not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Etched on the Pillars of Creation</span><br /> Cost:</b> 2m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Resonant, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mark of Reproeach, Border-Marking Stroke, any two other Evocations of Final Stroke<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant:</b> Only characters resonant with moonsilver can awaken this Evocation.<br /> <br /> The law dies only with the Lawgiver. Channeling her own Essence into Final Stroke's ink, the wielder renders her work ineffaceable so long as she maintains the commitment. Even if the writing surface is destroyed, the ghost of her words hovers beside the fragments. One use of this Charm can preserve several paragraphs of ordinary writing or a couple sentences of large-scale writing such as graffiti. Alternatively, one use sustains a Mark of Reproach or Boundary-Marking Stroke indefinitely. The Exalt must end this effect if she wishes to sacrifice the mark to fuel effects like Scorned God Retribution.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> After maintaining a commitment for a full year, the Exalt may drop it (and any supporting commitments, as from Border-Marking Stroke) to make the effect truly permanent. She can no longer sacrifice the mark after this, but it can be removed with a sorcerous working (Terrestrial Circle, Ambition 2) or by thoroughly destroying the underlying surface.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And while I'm <i>reasonably</i> happy with where this is at, in the spirit of the thread here are my thoughts on it as it stands:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Officially I think pens are <i>verboten</i>, but I found at least one or two references to quills so I'm gonna call it good. In the broadest sense this is hitting the same gimmick as Sun's Brush from Arms of the Chosen (which you might use as a foundation for your thing, BrilliantRain? It's a grimcleaver with a bunch of fact-introduction powers, after all), but the aesthetic is somewhat different and it's much more focused on writing rather than knowing.<br /> <br /> The Evocations were a bit fussy: in the spirit of a three-dot weapon they're more quality-of-life improvements than a paradigmatic &quot;style&quot;, but they're also <i>weird</i> effects. I feel OK about Mark of Reproach and Cutting Invective Assault, but I have <i>some</i> misgivings about Stinging Admonition just because it's virtually automatic damage. I decided it was OK because it's mostly just cashing in the Initiative spent on the gambit, and once someone knows about it they can just avoid reading things to keep it from triggering (and indeed illiteracy is a perfect defense!)<br /> <br /> Border-Marking Stroke was a lot of trouble, and it still has the most issues of anything here. I had a very precise idea of how I wanted this to function, but it was too complicated to write up, so the form shown here is greatly simplified (and even then it clocks in at 200 words, which is pushing it). In this form it requires a certain amount of negotiation or rapport between the player and Storyteller about what positioning is kosher. That being said, the best way to use it is to spend 15 minutes drawing a gigantic single-line maze over the entire battlefield before anybody else shows up, in which context the positioning considerations are a bit less severe.<br /> <br /> Scorned God Retribution is extremely strong, but I think it's OK simply because it uses up the marked border and those are a tremendous hassle to set up. (It also uses a noncombat dice pool just to mess with you.) I hope I made it explicit enough that this and the damage enhancer from Mark of Reproach <i>use up </i>their respective marks.<br /> <br /> Draw the Line is where 50% of the actual power of this thing comes from, after you have Mark of Reproach. This is bordering on too good, I think, given that you can trigger it just by scribbling &quot;PISS OFF&quot; on the walls before you get into a fight, but as with Stinging Admiration it's weak against people who don't or can't read things you put in front of them, and targets will often get a Resolve bonus in contexts where it matters. My main remaining misgiving is that if you use this all the time, as it incentivizes you to do, the indefinite duration of the effects means there could be a lot of bookkeeping. It didn't seem worth nerfing the duration on that account, however.<br /> <br /> Etched on the Pillars of Creation is the &quot;ult&quot;, but it's kind of a weird one because this is a weird weapon. The principle implied by Arms seems to be that three-dot stuff usually won't have a really dramatic ult, so I went with a quality-of-life improvement that opens up some wider possibilities for complicated shenanigans, but it is a little weird as the final super technique. Ess 4 might be overkill here, but it's not a trivial effect; I think it's on the cusp?<br /> <br /> I don't have too much to say about the splat-specific Evocations except that Fierce Heart Mandate is <i>maybe</i> a little too good, but it really just nudges Beast-King Dictates over the line from &quot;the last motes you spend&quot; to &quot;the first motes you spend&quot;, so I think it's probably OK if, as the learn condition suggests, the artifact is significant to your character.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-23-2020, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T06:08:44-07:00","id":1383947,"title":"","content":"so should the charm shapeshifting the armor into a warstrider sized thing be the highest charm? or should I keep going from there?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T22:24:35-07:00","id":1384107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1383947#post1383947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so should the charm shapeshifting the armor into a warstrider sized thing be the highest charm? or should I keep going from there?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>hmmm.... I\u2019d probably make that the highest one, yes. If it was a full on NA level, I might have a few Warstrider only evocations, but for a rank 5, being able to switch into a giant form is probably enough","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T07:28:52-07:00","id":1384189,"title":"","content":"White Shard Nodes.<br /> <br /> So 2.5 has a necromantic spell White Shard Funeral where the necromancer can see through any mirror they know the location of and communicate with people on the other side, with the option of adding more mirrors. The downside of the spell is that when it ends, all mirrors shatter.<br /> <br /> I am thinking of a specific artifact set; of mirrors composed of soulsteel and moonsilver, that are specifically linked at their creation. And which don't shatter when done.<br /> <br /> Would a whole set of say 5 mirrors be an artifact 4? And each mirror an artifact 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:41:38-07:00","id":1384232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1384189#post1384189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Shard Nodes.<br /> <br /> So 2.5 has a necromantic spell White Shard Funeral where the necromancer can see through any mirror they know the location of and communicate with people on the other side, with the option of adding more mirrors. The downside of the spell is that when it ends, all mirrors shatter.<br /> <br /> I am thinking of a specific artifact set; of mirrors composed of soulsteel and moonsilver, that are specifically linked at their creation. And which don't shatter when done.<br /> <br /> Would a whole set of say 5 mirrors be an artifact 4? And each mirror an artifact 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m going to note that, in 3e, connecting two minds to communicate across any distance is a Celestial 1 Working. As such, I could see these being the product of a Sorcerous Working, with some kind of weird activating ritual type thing going on. Similarly there are a number of terrestrial spells that allow communication over long distances.<br /> <br /> so, there\u2019s a part of me that would say, based on that, these could be artifact 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Creation does not have widespread long distance communication technology and all the methods it does have are limited in one way or another. If these things are in the artifact 2 range, then any artificer can make a set of them and that potentially changes the setting.<br /> <br /> So, I could see a few ways to go here. You say \u201cwell, it\u2019s my game and I\u2019m just gonna ignore that bit\u201d in which case, I\u2019d make them artifact 2. Or you go with the \u201cstandard method\u201d of marking that \u201cthis stuff does weird things to the setting\u201d and make them artifact 2 but give them the First Age Technology tag and some kind of regular maintenance ritual that needs to be done, lest the ghosts inside get unruly and cloud the mirror. Or, you say \u201cweeell, I don\u2019t wanna break the setting but First Age tech isn\u2019t where I wanna go with this either,\u201d in which case I\u2019d make them Artifact 4.<br /> <br /> Does that help at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:50:45-07:00","id":1384272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1384189#post1384189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Shard Nodes.<br /> <br /> So 2.5 has a necromantic spell White Shard Funeral where the necromancer can see through any mirror they know the location of and communicate with people on the other side, with the option of adding more mirrors. The downside of the spell is that when it ends, all mirrors shatter.<br /> <br /> I am thinking of a specific artifact set; of mirrors composed of soulsteel and moonsilver, that are specifically linked at their creation. And which don't shatter when done.<br /> <br /> Would a whole set of say 5 mirrors be an artifact 4? And each mirror an artifact 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>A White Shard Node is a dangerous thing to use.<br /> <br /> The are not all accounted for! We don't know who else might be watching","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:31:20-07:00","id":1389808,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a character right niw who I'm thinking of giving an aryifact fighting staff, and having that staff able to break down into paired batons. But I&quot;m worried aside from stunting potential, and the ability to go between MA styles, would this give any real advantage? Or would it be better to just make a regular wreckstaff ot baton pair?<br /> <br /> Also, are there any MA styles that use staffs. I know Golden Jannisary does, but going back through the published ones for 3E, and digging out SotM I didn't see others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T17:03:14-07:00","id":1390416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1389808#post1389808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a character right niw who I'm thinking of giving an aryifact fighting staff, and having that staff able to break down into paired batons. But I&amp;quot;m worried aside from stunting potential, and the ability to go between MA styles, would this give any real advantage? Or would it be better to just make a regular wreckstaff ot baton pair?<br /> <br /> Also, are there any MA styles that use staffs. I know Golden Jannisary does, but going back through the published ones for 3E, and digging out SotM I didn't see others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Laughing Monster and I believe White Reaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T22:25:50-07:00","id":1392759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1389808#post1389808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a character right niw who I'm thinking of giving an aryifact fighting staff, and having that staff able to break down into paired batons. But I&quot;m worried aside from stunting potential, and the ability to go between MA styles, would this give any real advantage? Or would it be better to just make a regular wreckstaff ot baton pair?<br /> <br /> Also, are there any MA styles that use staffs. I know Golden Jannisary does, but going back through the published ones for 3E, and digging out SotM I didn't see others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think there are any baton using styles yet, but, as far as staff styles go, in addition to the ones noted above, there\u2019s Wood Dragon in the DB book and Celestial Monkey is going to be in the Lunars Companion. You could maybe argue that paired batons would qualify for Steel Devil style, but....<br /> <br /> Oh! Swaying Grass Dance and Mantis allow for Batons.<br /> <br /> So, technically, probably sticking with the Wrackstaff is fine? Unless you want to practice White Reaper with Swaying Grass or something.<br /> <br /> That said, if you like the idea of a staff that can separate out into a set of batons (or maybe it can pop out into a seven section staff), go for it. You can make some evocations that let you do cool stuff with the batons even without a particular MA style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T21:34:02-07:00","id":1392996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1392759#post1392759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So, technically, probably sticking with the Wrackstaff is fine? Unless you want to practice White Reaper with Swaying Grass or something.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, out of what's out now WR and SGD fit best. Though, can easily put this on a back burner and wait for new ones to come out since this is for a Sidereal concept","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T12:38:15-07:00","id":1393488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1392996#post1392996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, out of what's out now WR and SGD fit best. Though, can easily put this on a back burner and wait for new ones to come out since this is for a Sidereal concept</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s probably a good idea since Sids isn\u2019t out yet, but I\u2019m curious what thoughts you had about any other powers for the artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T18:53:51-07:00","id":1393565,"title":"","content":"I'm really not sure. I suck at evocations and charm invention in general. But, as this is for a martial artist and most MAs don't use armor maybe abilities that boost defense would be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T20:37:34-07:00","id":1394709,"title":"","content":"I've got a custom Artifact for you all! this one is tied to my character, a Solar Weaponsmith. In and out of game its based on Alveua's Forge of Night.<br /> <br /> I had a problem with Artifact Creation rules, namely that anything you want to make takes weeks or months with the right charms, or years without (<i>but you can just start with Artifact 5 so why even bother investing in Craft to make them urrrgh)</i>. So like a good crafter I crafted a solution to the problem: <b>\u200bDisposable Artifacts!</b> (<i>gasp) </i>The Twilight Salzan is never satisfied with any design and is always eager to move on to the next thing, and he learned from his master Alveua the technique of forging sapients into more useful things, like swords.<br /> <br /> The <b>Unstable</b> keyword (I couldn't think of a better name) lets Salzan say a word or phrase and then destroy his own artifact for power, something that seems like plagiarism familiar to all of you Fate Series fans. Then fueled by inspiration, he makes a new one one.<br /> <br /> Without further ado, behold the <u><b>Black Anvil</b></u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>The Black Anvil</b> Artifact 3<br /> Attunement: 5m<br /> <br /> <i>Forged in a leyline of Malfeas, the <b>Black Anvil</b> is a Sorcerous Focus as much as it is a tool of Crafting. To it's maker Salzan, they're are practically the same thing. </i><br /> <br /> Unique Keyword: <i><u>Unstable</u></i>. This effect triggers on the Artifact's destruction.<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> <br /> <i><u>At Beck and Call</u> </i><br /> While the Black Anvil irrevocably a part of the realm of Malfeas, it neither exists there or in Creation: it belongs to soul of it's Master, and therein it resides. This evocation allows you to summon and dismiss the <b>Black Anvil</b> from your soul by attuning to it (5m). Additionally, the <b>Black Anvil</b> always counts as the relevant tools for any crafting project- hammer, tongs, whetstone, saw, vice, etc.<br /> <br /> <i><u>Malfean Resources</u> </i><br /> The realm of Malfeas is as bountiful as it is wicked. A demon of the First Circle may be sacrificed on the <b>Black Anvil</b> and turned into the hellish material known as <i>Corrupted Brass</i>. A single demon produces one large ingot of this metal, enough for a man-sized weapon or suit of armor. Any excess material dissolves back into essence after the projects completion.<br /> <br /> <i><u>Experimental Design</u></i><br /> Owning to it's creator's insatiable lust to always move on to the next design, and the cavalier disregard he has for the lives of demons, Artifacts forged on the <b>Black Anvil</b> may bear the Keyword <i>Unstable</i>. An Unstable artifact can be willingly destroyed by invoking a secret means, and this action will produce an effect of incredible -usually destructive- power. The effects depend on the artifact.<br /> <br /> <i><u>Replacing the Irreplaceable</u></i><br /> Destruction breeds Creation. After analyzing the strengths and weaknesses of a previous design, inspiration for the next one leaps to mind. If Salzan has destroyed an artifact by using the Unstable effect, he may build a new artifact of a similar type with only a single scene of downtime crafting. May switch weapon type, light/medium/heavy. <b>May only be used to make another Unstable artifact</b>.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> Ligier's Hatred- Artifact Spear, Corrupted Brass.<br /> Concept: Lazer Cannon + Short Spear<br /> Unstable: will detonate after being thrown, sending the Green Sun's scorching rays in all directions. Deals # Aggravated damage as an environmental effect to everyone up to short range at the beginning of Salzan's next turn.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought it was a pretty elegant work around to the limit of how long Artifact creation rules are, and how seriously Exalted takes Artifacts as weapons of Legend. The idea for Salzan is that each artifact weapon is like a proof of concept prototype, not a relic of power to last for millennium. Ligier's Hatred is there just to give you an idea of what an Unstable effect might look like- in this case, a laser shooting spear would explode into a laser death blossom like a grenade. <i>Replacing the Irreplaceable </i> gives you the freedom to change the weapon type, so after the Spear explodes you might make a Fiery Axe or a Sword that eats darkness. Generally speaking, its Melee Weapon to any other Melee Weapon, Ranged to Ranged, Armor to Armor. Although I don't plan on making much armor.<br /> <br /> My goal was to have an master smith of artifact weapons able to make new and exciting artifacts all the time, but without destroying the setting expectation for what artifacts are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 06-07-2020, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T00:19:49-07:00","id":1394732,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... I\u2019d probably assert that\u2019s a level 5 artifact. I could see arguing for it to be N/A, since you\u2019re kind of rewriting the game\u2019s rules, but the Unstable keyword seems like a good way to prevent anything from getting too crazy.<br /> <br /> You might want to note how that interacts with Evocations though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T02:32:04-07:00","id":1394738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372903-artifact-workshop?p=1394732#post1394732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.... I\u2019d probably assert that\u2019s a level 5 artifact. I could see arguing for it to be N/A, since you\u2019re kind of rewriting the game\u2019s rules, but the Unstable keyword seems like a good way to prevent anything from getting too crazy.<br /> <br /> You might want to note how that interacts with Evocations though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback, its my first draft. The sort of informal agreement I have with my ST is that I only have one Unstable artifact at a time, to represent the way Salzan is always going through them like the Mad Tortured Genius he is. <br /> <br /> I originally was going to dismantle my Artifact du Jour and remake it when Salzan got tired of it, and I had a different idea about sacrificing my creations to generate Sorcerous Motes and i decided to fuse them into the concept of a disposable artifact. <br /> <br /> As for Evocations of the Unstable Artifacts, it basically is an Evocation unlocked for free. With the craft charm that unlocks an evocation when you make something, I figure I can have 1 evocation and 1 Unstable effect per weapon, which is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T09:36:17-07:00","id":1394788,"title":"","content":"My Twilight is working on a caudlron of nurgle artefact that would make sorcerous workings for brewing deseases and cures workings easier and also keep stuff like soup warm and stir itself and follow him around dripping soup on its metal legs kinda like the luggage from Terry Pratchets Discworld. I want to use it to make killing the trees of those Haltan dicks easier. And Maybe giving explosive diarhea to the mean citizens of Lookshy.<br /> <br /> Althought it might be easier to do it in two stages one is the desease brewing artefact and 2 celestial working to make it sentient and walk around . So as not to make the diffuculty of making the artefact too high. The ST still hasnt got back to me as to how difficult it would be to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 06-07-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T09:42:14-07:00","id":1394790,"title":"","content":"One of my players requested a combination weapon, a spear/firewand/seven section staff:<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Lashing Dragon\u2019s Tail (***)</u></b><br /> It was the pinnacle creation of an order of warrior monks that trained extensively to use it. It was used previously as the weapon of enforcement by a corrupt king and this is the last remaining one, as the rest were destroyed when his reign ended. It is decorated with alternating red and green patterns, suggesting a dragon's fire and dragon's scales. When the blunt end is spun, it makes a roaring sound. When not in use, it is worn like a bandolier, shoulder to waist, with one end locked into the other. It's also known as an Ouroboros Spear for this appearance.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement</b>: 5m<br /> <b>Hearthstone Slot(s)</b>: 1<br /> <br /> EVOCATIONS OF THE LASHING DRAGON\u2019S TAIL<br /> The Lashing Dragon\u2019s Tail is a curious weapon. Superficially it is a serpent-sting staff made of green and red jade, but a closer inspection reveals its secret. One tip of the weapon boasts a lethally sharp spearhead; the other conceals the barrel and firing mechanisms of a firewand. By reflexively spending 1m, the wielder can cause the seven segments of the staff to fuse together in different ways, allowing it to be used as a spear, staff, or firewand. The different configurations are:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lashing Tail</u></b><ul><li><b>Type</b>: Medium (+12 damage, +1 Defense, overwhelming 4)</li> <li><b>Accuracy</b>: +3</li> <li><b>Tags</b>: Bashing, Martial Arts, Disarming, Flexible, Reaching</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Ouroboros Spear</u></b><ul><li><b>Type</b>: Medium (+12 damage, +1 Defense, overwhelming 4)</li> <li><b>Accuracy</b>: +3</li> <li><b>Tags</b>: Lethal, Melee, Thrown (Short), Piercing</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Spine of Eternity</u></b><ul><li><b>Type</b>: Medium (+12 damage, +1 Defense, overwhelming 4)</li> <li><b>Accuracy</b>: +3</li> <li><b>Tags</b>: Bashing, Melee, Reaching</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Breath of the Dragon</u></b><ul><li><b>Type</b>: Heavy (+14 damage, overwhelming 5)</li> <li><b>Accuracy</b>: Close -1, Short +5, Medium +3, Long +1, Extreme -1</li> <li><b>Tags</b>: Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Slow</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>ENCIRCLING TAIL</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> The Lashing Tail\u2019s links are quick to catch at enemy limbs and blades. This Evocation allows the wielder to make a disarm or grapple gambit as a counterattack, after the attack is rolled but before damage is rolled. This doesn\u2019t count as her combat action for the round, and every threshold success on the attack roll adds one bonus die on the Initiative roll for the gambit.<br /> If the Lashing Dragon Tail\u2019s is not in its Lashing Tail conformation, it transforms as part of the counterattack.<br /> <br /> <b>OUROBOROS STRIKE</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> The flight of the Ouroboros Spear cannot be stopped. This Evocation allows you to pierce through one target and strike another. Make a <b>decisive</b> attack against a target at close range. If you hit, roll damage as normal and make a second attack against a second target in close range of the first one. To determine the damage of this second attack, reroll all non-successes from the first damage roll.<br /> If the Lashing Dragon Tail\u2019s is not in its Ouroboros Strike conformation, it transforms as part of the Simple action.<br /> <br /> <b>ENDURING STANCE TECHNIQUE</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> The Spine of Eternity can absorb and redirect even the strongest of blows. This Evocation grants +1 Parry against one attack. If you successfully block, you may cause your attacker to move one range band in any direction.<br /> If the Lashing Dragon Tail\u2019s is not in its Spine of Eternity conformation, it transforms as part of the parry.<br /> <br /> <b>BURNING INHALATION</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Dissonant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> As the wielder fires the Breath of the Dragon, a breeze draws fresh grains of firedust from her ammunition pouch into its barrel. Activating this Evocation reloads the weapon without an action.<br /> If the Lashing Dragon Tail\u2019s is not in its Breath of the Dragon conformation, it transforms as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T01:15:53-07:00","id":1412694,"title":"","content":"After playing for over a year, I finally got to creating evocations for my artifact. This is my first draft, so commentary and critique would be appreciated. I'm planning to add some more evocations, up to at least Essence 4, but am uncertain how I'd like to shape the tree \u2013 either an cross, with the next evocation requiring both of the Ess 2 ones, and then that allowing the upper two arms, or two parallel paths, with two combining evocations after the Ess 2 and 4 ones.<br /> I haven't checked the newer materials if Wavecleavers are their own thing in 3rd ed, but this would probably be one if they are. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Surface Current</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Black Jade Reaper Daiklave, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> Although Surface Current is known to be older, the first reliable records of it are from when the Empress donated it to a grandchild of Ledaal, as part of the hoard of her gifts to the newly founded house. Ledaal Valevuo carried it for many years, passing it on to a worthy younger relative when she retired from active duty. It was last seen in the hands of Ledaal Uhskals on his trip to investigate the Skullstone Archipelago, but he escaped with barely his life, and has been tight-lipped about what happened to him on his trip. Since then, there are tales of an newly exalted solar carrying it after his trip to the Skullstones, but these have not been confirmed.<br /> <br /> Surface Current is a gently curving blade made of black jade, with faint moonsliver waves traveling along the blade. Earlier records state that the guard separating the blade and grip was a small band of orichalcum and soulsteel, but according to the latest rumours, the hilt is now guarded by a small soulsteel cup. It has two hearthestone slots, one in the pommel and one hidden by the cup.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b> 5m<br /> <b>Type:</b> Medium (+3 ACC, +12 DMG, +1 DEF, OVW 5)<br /> <b>Tags:</b> Lethal, Melee, Balanced<br /> <b>Hearthstone slot:</b> 2<br /> <b>Era:</b> Late Shogunate?<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Surface Current</b><br /><br /> Surface Current carries it's wielder above things that might impede others, notably unstable or moving surfaces, or swiftly flowing fluids. A character attuned to Surface Current ignores all penalties from such things, and when activating charms that would counteract them (such as Graceful Crane Stance, Feather Foot Style, or using Increasing Strength Exercise to stride through a flooding river), their activation cost is decreased by 2 (to a minimum of 1 mote).<br /> <br /> <b>Swinging Deck Vertigo</b><br /><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Resonant, Withering-Only, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> When Surface Current connects with an opponent, a pulse of essence pushes through them, down their legs and on to the bottom of their feet, keeping them off-balance. If the withering damage done was greater than the (Essence) of the opponent, they suffer a special -1 onslaught penalty that lasts as long as the wielder keeps the opponent as their primary focus. This effect is cumulative, up to the wielder's (Essence) in penalties, but it does decrease by one each turn that the wielder does not act against that opponent.<br /> <b>Resonant:</b> At Essence 2+, the penalty is applied when the wielder lowers their opponent below their own initiative, even if the damage was not greater than the opponents (Essence).<br /> <br /> <b>Railing-Colliding Nausea</b><br /><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Swinging Deck Vertigo<br /> <br /> On a surging, slippery deck, the land-lubber is more likely to hurt themself than others. If you successfully parry, your opponent loses 1 initiative as you slowly turn the tide of the battle against them.<br /> <br /> <b>Mendaciously Smooth Shorewaters</b><br /><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Resonant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One turn<br /> <br /> Using Surface Current teaches one to not show one's intentions clearly. When the wielder knows they are being targeted by an Read Intentions action, they may activate Mendaciously Smooth Shorewaters to gain +2 to their Guile until the end of their next turn.<br /> <b>Resonant:</b> The wielder may also activate Mendaciously Smooth Shorewaters as a supplemental charm with an instant duration when making gambits based on deception, such as Distract. The difficulty of the Gambit is lowered by 2, to a minimum of 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Rip-Current Deception</b><br /><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1Wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Resonant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mendaciously Smooth Shorewaters<br /> <br /> Though the surface may be calm, the undercurrents can be fierce. When your opponent fails in their Read Intentions, you may activate this charm to give them a false motivation or Intimacy that they will believe to be true. Their belief will be sustained until it causes them to fail in a social action that should have succeeded, they see you act counter to what they read from you, or they spend 1 Wp to accept that they have been deceived.<br /> <b>Resonant:</b> You may pay 5m instead of 1 Wp as the cost.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1361-amoeba","name":"Amoeba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1361_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T18:13:21-07:00","id":1412939,"title":"","content":"The Dealer's Gambit (Decks of Adamant-Edged Cards, Artifact *)<br /> <br /> <br /> Fluff Goes Here! First age Eclipse! Invented the Fivefold Deck. Went a little crazy and made this before trying for the Games of Divinity. Peach-blend playing cards made from the trees of immortality, all five magical materials and adamant.<br /> <br /> Each of the five decks of the Dealer's Gambit is made of 67 perfectly illustrated and exceedingly fine cards, roughly the size of a man's hand. The card faces are purest white, with symbols and decorations of the finest quality. They are coated in an incredibly thin layer of adamant. This makes the cards unable to be bent, marked, or defaced, though they are flexible enough once attuned.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Attunement: 6 motes<br /> <br /> Type: Thrown Special (+9 DMG, OVW 1)<br /> <br /> Tags; Lethal, Thrown (Short), Concealable, Cutting, Mounted<br /> <br /> Accuracy: Close +4, Short +3, Medium +2, Long -1, Extreme -3<br /> <br /> Hearthstone Slot(s): None<br /> <br /> Era: Dawn of the Deliberative<br /> <br /> Special: Each of the five decks that make up the Dealer's Gambit is backed with a different magical material. They modify the statistics above for any deck of which they contribute to the Count.<br /> <br /> Orichalcum: Accuracy +1, +1 Overwhelming<br /> <br /> Moonsilver: Overwhelming +2<br /> <br /> Starmetal: Thrown (Medium)<br /> <br /> Jade: Damage +1, Overwhelming +1<br /> <br /> Soulsteel: Damage +4.<br /> <br /> Each deck resonates based on the material it is backed with.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> Evocations of the Dealer's Gambit<br /> <br /> Counting Cards: A single deck has a Count of 1. Each additional deck added increases the Count by 1, and the attunement cost by 1.<br /> <br /> Resonant: If you are resonant with the materials used for a deck, do not increase the attunement cost for adding that deck to the Count.<br /> <br /> Winnable Evocations: If you defeat a significant adversary who is carrying one of the decks in either a game involving them or in Combat, you may unlock one winnable Evocation for which you qualify (including the one for their deck, should you end the contest owning it). This does not have to be in a lethal contest, but the stakes must be significant (a body part, significant resources, an Artifact or an onerous task, for instance). Friendly games or sparring matches without consequence do not count. <br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Dealer's Shuffle<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 motes, or 3m 1 WP Mins: Essence 1<br /> <br /> Type: Simple<br /> <br /> Keywords: Dissonant, Resonant, (Winnable)<br /> <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> This causes each of the cards of the deck you are attuned to to vanish Elsewhere, and then re-appear randomized before you. This will have the side effect of retrieving cards which have been lost, stolen or palmed from the scene around him. This can be treated as an automatically successful gather ammunition action.<br /> By spending a WP this extends the effect to everywhere, even from a Sorceror's Tower, Elsewhere, Yu-Shan, the Wyld, Malfeas, the Underworld, or anywhere else the missing cards may happen to be.<br /> <br /> If you own two decks, you may Shuffle them into a single deck, increasing the Count to the total of both decks. You may also Shuffle a deck with a Count of more than 1 into component decks.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: So long as the Exalt isn't dissonant with the deck, this Evocation awakens at no cost when the deck is attuned.<br /> <br /> Resonant: The wielder may pay 1 WP when involved in a game with someone attuned to another of the five decks of the Dealer's Gambit. If they do so, they benefit from any of the Essence 1 Evocations anyone in the game has awakened.<br /> <br /> Dissonant: If the Exalt is dissonant to the deck, he makes this Evocation winnable, but does not automatically awaken it upon attunement.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> The Arcana of the Most High<br /> <br /> Cost: -- Mins: Essence 1, Count 1<br /> <br /> Type: Permanent<br /> <br /> Keywords: Winnable<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Dealer's Shuffle, Your Count must contain the Orichalcum cards.<br /> <br /> Heaven itself enforces bets made with these cards. Anyone who refuses to pay or offer what they have wagered in a game using the Dealer's Gambit suffers a number of botches equal to the Count of the deck, exactly as if the bet had been sanctified by an Eclipse. These botches STACK with those of such an Oath, if an Eclipse or Moonshadow has also sanctified the terms of the wager.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> The Fickle Faces of Luna<br /> <br /> Cost: -- Mins: Essence 1, Count 1<br /> <br /> Type: Permanent<br /> <br /> Keywords: Winnable<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Dealer's Shuffle, Your Count must contain the Moonsilver cards.<br /> <br /> These cards give a liar's nature. Add the Count to your Socialize for the purpose of rolling your Read Intentions actions and calculating Guile while playing with the Dealer's Gambit. This is a Non-Charm dice bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> The Maidens' Hand<br /> <br /> Cost: -- Mins: Essence 1, Count 1<br /> <br /> Type: Permanent<br /> <br /> Keywords: Winnable<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Dealer's Shuffle, Your Count must contain the Starmetal cards.<br /> <br /> These cards remove the possibility of disaster. Any time you make a roll involving the Dealer's Gambit (in combat or card play), remove a number of dice showing '1' from your roll equal to the Count. This happens before any opponent charms that use those 1s, or the calculation of botches, but after any of your charm effects that may reroll them.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> The Elemental Array<br /> <br /> Cost: -- Mins: Essence 1, Count 1<br /> <br /> Type: Permanent<br /> <br /> Keywords: Winnable<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Dealer's Shuffle, Your Count must contain the Jade cards.<br /> <br /> These cards give the owner a preternatural insight into cheating. Add a number of Non-Charm succeses equal to the Count to any Awareness, Investigation, or Larceny ability rolls involving the Dealer's Gambit. Any normally unrolled attempt to oppose these skills with the Dealer's Gambit immediately becomes contested, unless it comes from an effect with a higher essence than your essence + the Count.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> The Dead Man's Draw<br /> <br /> Cost: -- Mins: Essence 1, Count 1<br /> <br /> Type: Permanent<br /> <br /> Keywords: Winnable<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Dealer's Shuffle, Your Count must contain the Soulsteel cards.<br /> <br /> The dread stasis of the Underworld drains outside influences from the players of these cards. Astrological effects that try to predict or affect the players fail, when it comes to the use of the Dealer's Gambit. (It may be your Dark Fate to be stabbed over a hand of cards, but the cards will fall as they may, without outside interference) Any other manipulation of luck except that of the Dealer's Gambit or the charms of the players themselves, such as a divine blessing or curse, an Eclipse Sanctified Oath, or any other such effect also fails to affect players for the purposes of the game, even fiat level manipulation of the loom of fate. (A blessing that made you a supernaturally skilled liar might still help you win a card game incorporating bluffing, but one that made you lucky would not).<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Five Elements Understanding<br /> <br /> Cost: 4 motes, 1WP Mins: Essence 3, Count 3<br /> <br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Keywords: Understanding<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: The Elemental Array, Your Count must contain the Jade cards<br /> <br /> Treat all ranges as if they were one category closer when attacking with the Dealer's Gambit. This includes maximum range, as well as when aiming is required, and accuracy bonuses. If you already have an Understanding active when you use this charm, remove the WP cost of this charm, and replace that understanding with this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Destiny Understanding<br /> <br /> Cost: 4 motes, 1WP Mins: Essence 3, Count 3<br /> <br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Keywords: Understanding<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: The Maidens' Hand, Your Count must contain the Starmetal cards<br /> <br /> Add a success to any opposed roll involving the Dealer's Gambit for each 10 or 1 an opponent's roll shows. If you already have an Understanding active when you use this charm, remove the WP cost of this charm, and replace that understanding with this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Underworld Understanding<br /> <br /> Cost: 4 motes, 1WP Mins: Essence 3, Count 3<br /> <br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Keywords: Understanding<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: The Dead Man's Draw, Your Count must contain the Soulsteel cards<br /> <br /> Your attacks with the deck can affect dematerialized spirits. If you cannot see them, you take a -3 to the attack as normal. If you already have an Understanding active when you use this charm, remove the WP cost of this charm, and replace that understanding with this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Wyld Understanding<br /> <br /> Cost: 4 motes, 1WP Mins: Essence 3, Count 3<br /> <br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Keywords: Understanding<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: The Fickle Faces of Luna, Your Count must contain the Moonsilver cards<br /> <br /> 1/scene if you have this Understanding active before you roll, you may reroll ANY roll involving the Dealer's Gambit (including damage). Any charms you used are used again for free on this reroll, but any opponent's charms must be reused at cost. This Evocation can not be reset. If you already have an Understanding active when you use this charm, remove the WP cost of this charm, and replace that understanding with this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Divine Understanding<br /> <br /> Cost: 4 motes, 1WP Mins: Essence 3, Count 3<br /> <br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Keywords: Understanding<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: The Arcana of the Most High, Your Count must contain the Orichalcum cards<br /> <br /> You gain double 9s on any roll you make involving the Dealer's Gambit. If you already have double 9s (or better) add 1 to the range of doubles. If you already have an Understanding active when you use this charm, remove the WP cost of this charm, and replace that understanding with this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> Perfected Fivefold Understanding of Creation<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 WP Mins: Essence 4, Count 5<br /> <br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Keywords: Decisive<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Divine Understanding, Wyld Understanding, Destiny Understanding, Underworld Understanding, Five Elements Understanding<br /> <br /> To understand a thing is to know how to destroy it. Attacks with the deck ignore hardness, and affect legendary creatures as if they did not have the benefits of the merit for restricting damage. They ignore any effect that would reduce the damage of a successful attack with the Dealer's Gambit below the Count before it is rolled. While this Understanding is active, you may spend 1 WP before making a decisive attack, if you do the attack does aggravated damage. While the Fivefold Understanding is active, all other understandings cost 1 WP and 2 motes less, and may all be active simultaneously.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> Interested Parties and the Dealer's Gambit:<br /> <br /> The Orichalcum Deck was buried with the Solar who held it during the Usurpation, somewhere in the Scavenger Lands. Members of the Cult of the Illuminated have been asking about it.<br /> <br /> The Moonsilver Deck was held by Luranume for a time, though about ten years ago he lost it to a young changing moon, White Gloved Jack.<br /> <br /> The Starmetal Deck has changed hands many times, but last was seen in the hands of Nara-O, head of the Forbidding Manse of Ivy, some 63 years ago. He has almost certainly given it to someone to use since then, but of course, exactly who is a secret.<br /> <br /> The Jade Deck has been in and out of the hands of Plentimon of the Dice multiple times over the last century. He is able to share the magic of the deck through his divine powers, and seems particularly fond of catching unaware Dragonblooded trying to cheat him with it. He never keeps it for long, however, and last report had it in the hands of a young Lieutenant from House Peleps.<br /> <br /> The Soulsteel Deck was in the possession of a Sijanese noble dead, before his brutal end at the hands of a deathknight claiming allegiance to The Empress of Whispers. Sages are unsure if this is a reclusive and relatively unknown Deathlord, or another guise for one of them that is already known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}